## Plan: Frontend-Backend Integration

Wire the Next.js UI to the existing Go backend through the BFF proxy, map backend DTOs to UI models, preserve the current look and feel, and keep placeholders only as complements to backend data where fields do not exist (category/image/plays/leaderboard/admin stats). No backend or BFF changes.

**Steps**
1. Preflight constraints and contracts
   - Follow the Next.js rule in AGENTS.md to read the required guide before frontend edits.
   - Confirm `GO_BACKEND_URL` and session cookie settings used by the BFF; all backend calls must go through the proxy route.
   - Review backend schemas in Swagger to confirm request/response shapes for quizzes, attempts, and submissions.
2. Define UI-to-backend mapping helpers (parallel with step 3)
   - Create mapping logic for `QuizDTO` → UI quiz cards: derive `status` from `publish_date` and `is_archived`, map `question_count`, convert `time_limit_seconds` → minutes.
   - Keep placeholders only for fields the backend cannot supply (category, image, plays/attempts count, leaderboard, admin stats) and always render real backend values for title/description/time limits/status.
3. Auth and role gating
   - Use `requireAuth()` on protected pages (`/dashboard`, `/quizzes`, `/attempts/*`, `/admin/*`).
   - Use `getSessionUser()` to enforce admin-only pages; handle 403 with a minimal “not authorized” state.
4. Page-by-page integration
   - Dashboard: fetch recent attempts from `/api/users/me/submissions`; map to “recent attempts” cards. Build “recommended quizzes” from latest published quizzes (list endpoint), limited to the current UI count. Keep admin stats/actions placeholders.
   - Quizzes list: fetch `/api/quizzes` (published scope where supported) and map to cards; keep category/image/plays placeholders; wire filters to available fields only.
   - Quiz detail: fetch `/api/quizzes/{id}/info` for metadata; keep leaderboard placeholder; when starting an attempt, fetch `/api/quizzes/{id}` to get questions and options.
   - Attempt player: start attempt via `POST /api/quizzes/{id}/attempts`; on selection send `PATCH /api/quizzes/{id}/attempts` updates; finish via `POST /api/quizzes/{id}/attempts/finish`. Handle 409 (already started) by redirecting to result or showing resume state.
   - Attempt result: fetch `GET /api/quizzes/{id}/attempts` for results and join with quiz questions/answers from `/api/quizzes/{id}` to display text, correctness, and points.
   - Admin list: use `/api/quizzes` and derive status; keep attempts count placeholder where missing.
   - Admin detail/new: wire create/update flows to `POST /api/quizzes`, `PUT /api/quizzes/{id}`, `POST /api/quizzes/{id}/questions`, `PUT /api/questions/{questionId}`, `DELETE /api/questions/{questionId}`, and publish/archive endpoints. Keep UI intact.
5. Replace mock data usages
   - Remove `mock-data` imports where backend data now exists.
   - Only use placeholders to fill missing fields after mapping real backend data (category/image/plays/leaderboard/admin stats); never override backend values.
6. Error handling and UX guardrails
   - Handle 401 by redirecting to login; handle 403 with access denied; show simple empty states for 404s or empty lists.
   - Ensure loading states do not shift layout significantly (minimal visual changes).
7. Persist the plan file in the repo root after approval using the provided filename.

